ArchiveEntry "Complete parametric pH Lyapunov certificate (V>0 AND V'<0), general D1,K"

/*
 * COMPLETE parametric Level-A certificate (corrected: includes D1>b).
 * Two-machine pH system, D1>0, K>0, D2=-d (d=|D2|>0).
 *
 * V = H + h*sin^2(delta) + a1*w1*sin(delta) + a2*w2*sin(delta),
 *   a1=D1+d, a2=(D1+3d)/2, h=(6D1^2+11D1 d+15d^2)/32.
 *
 * CONDITION (corrected): D1 > d  AND  (2*D1+3*d)^2 < 16*K.
 * (D1>d was missing from earlier prose; it appears as the (D1-d) factor in
 *  the V'-minors and is the trace/Routh requirement a2=D1-d>0.)
 *
 * V is a Lyapunov function iff BOTH:
 *   (i)  V > 0: P_full=[[1,0,a1/2],[0,1,a2/2],[a1/2,a2/2,K+h]] positive definite.
 *        Leading minors: 1, 1, (32K-4D1^2-17D1 d-11d^2)/32.
 *   (ii) V' < 0: -M(1) positive definite (linearized at c=1).
 *        Leading minors: D1-d, 7(D1-d)^2/16, 7(D1-d)^3(16K-(2D1+3d)^2)/512.
 *
 * Both sets of minors are > 0 under the condition. This QE proves it for
 * ALL D1,K,d. (Combines the V>0 check, missing before, with V'<0.)
 *
 * SCOPE: this is the Level-A (fixed-coefficient) sharp threshold. It is
 * STRICTER than the true stability boundary (Level C: D1>d AND K>D1 d):
 * at K=D1 d the condition (2D1+3d)^2<16K fails since (2D1+3d)^2-16 D1 d
 * = 4D1^2-4D1 d+9d^2 = (2D1-d)^2+8d^2 > 0 always. So Level A never reaches
 * Level C; the gap is intrinsic to this fixed energy-correction ansatz.
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real D1;
  Real K;
  Real d;
End.

Problem
  \forall D1 \forall K \forall d (
    ( D1 > 0 & K > 0 & d > 0 & d < D1 & (2*D1+3*d)^2 < 16*K )
    ->
    (   /* (i) V > 0 : P_full positive definite */
        32*K - 4*D1^2 - 17*D1*d - 11*d^2 > 0
      & /* (ii) V' < 0 : -M(1) positive definite */
        D1 - d > 0
      & 7*(D1-d)^2/16 > 0
      & 7*(D1-d)^3*(16*K-(2*D1+3*d)^2)/512 > 0 ) )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  QE
End.

End.
